WEBVTT

00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:06.140
W-What?!

00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:08.540
D-Don't mess with me!

00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:12.210
I was the one who won!

00:00:12.210 --> 00:00:16.080
Why is Taira's article so much bigger?!

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:18.640
Pops!

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:20.300
Is he that incredible?

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:23.970
Hey, how about it, Pops?

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:34.060
Then I'll ask you, Ryou.

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:41.530
Would you have the confidence to beat him
 if he drove the same kart as you?

00:01:03.130 --> 00:01:04.170
<i>What?!</i>

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:37.540
<i>I won against a guy who was on a three-year-old kart...</i>

00:01:48.670 --> 00:01:49.780
Taira!

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:37.910
You sure you're okay with this?

00:03:38.600 --> 00:03:39.480
Yes.

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:42.670
It's going to be too late to regret it later, you know.

00:03:43.750 --> 00:03:45.150
I'm fine.

00:03:45.150 --> 00:03:46.670
I've made up my mind.

00:03:49.140 --> 00:03:50.360
Okay.

00:03:50.360 --> 00:03:51.380
Then let's go.

00:04:22.870 --> 00:04:24.000
All right!

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:25.440
Way to go, Isamu!

00:04:25.440 --> 00:04:26.750
Keep it up!

00:04:27.230 --> 00:04:29.560
Isamu is driving well today.

00:04:29.560 --> 00:04:33.060
He'll be able to aim for the win for sure this time.

00:04:33.060 --> 00:04:34.380
You're right.

00:04:38.600 --> 00:04:41.640
<b>A devastating course-out by the leader, Tobita!</b>

00:04:41.640 --> 00:04:43.430
<b>Can he get back on the course?!</b>

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:47.550
<b>The lead has changed to Shiba in the 19th lap!</b>

00:04:49.620 --> 00:04:52.000
<i>I'm not going to...</i>

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:54.070
<i>I'm not going to make that kind of mistake again!</i>

00:05:00.340 --> 00:05:05.430
<b>Car #22, Tobita Isamu from Autohouse, has achieved the top time already!</b>

00:05:05.430 --> 00:05:07.210
All right!

00:05:05.820 --> 00:05:07.210
<b>50.159 seconds!</b>

00:05:07.600 --> 00:05:10.710
I was worried that his mistake at Haruna would influence his driving...

00:05:10.710 --> 00:05:13.920
but fortunately, he's trying to use it to bounce back and improve.

00:05:13.920 --> 00:05:18.250
Isamu sure has grown, Manager.

00:05:18.250 --> 00:05:19.390
You're right.

00:05:20.380 --> 00:05:21.940
<i>What is it...</i>

00:05:21.940 --> 00:05:25.000
<i>There's nothing going wrong...</i>

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:27.850
<i>but why do I feel like something's missing?</i>

00:05:37.730 --> 00:05:39.270
Monami!

00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:46.430
I made too much oden yesterday, so could you please take some to Ca-chan's place?

00:05:46.430 --> 00:05:47.590
Okay.

00:05:53.880 --> 00:05:55.090
Yummy!

00:06:01.010 --> 00:06:05.220
<i>I'm going to win this time, no matter what.</i>

00:06:07.690 --> 00:06:08.950
<i>Who is it?!</i>

00:06:10.620 --> 00:06:12.360
<i>Car #7.</i>

00:06:12.360 --> 00:06:13.580
<i>It's Shiba!</i>

00:06:15.110 --> 00:06:17.030
<b>Car #7.</b>

00:06:17.030 --> 00:06:18.990
<b>Garage Hill's Shiba Ryou.</b>

00:06:18.990 --> 00:06:24.100
<b>He easily overwrites Autohouse's Tobita Isamu's time.</b>

00:06:24.910 --> 00:06:26.620
All right!

00:06:25.960 --> 00:06:30.120
<b>His time is 50.011 seconds.</b>

00:06:27.950 --> 00:06:30.120
<i>That's how it should be, Ryou.</i>

00:06:30.120 --> 00:06:37.470
<i>The reason why you couldn't improve your level of driving was because you lacked that fighting spirit.</i>

00:06:37.470 --> 00:06:41.930
<i>Especially after Minamoto Naomi went up to the FA.</i>

00:06:41.930 --> 00:06:45.890
<i>You need to have rivals in order to make your fighting spirit burn.</i>

00:06:45.890 --> 00:06:49.310
<i>And that's when Taira Capeta appeared.</i>

00:06:51.480 --> 00:06:53.940
<i>Taira has set Ryou on fire.</i>

00:06:57.490 --> 00:07:01.490
<i>You can't stop Ryou once he's started.</i>

00:06:59.770 --> 00:07:03.450
<b>Shiba's driving has broken its old limits!</b>

00:07:03.450 --> 00:07:05.450
<b>He's way in the lead.</b>

00:07:15.710 --> 00:07:17.300
Ca-chan, you there?

00:07:18.760 --> 00:07:21.260
My mom's sent over some oden.

00:07:23.970 --> 00:07:26.110
You sick perverted old man!

00:07:26.110 --> 00:07:26.900
No, wait!

00:07:26.900 --> 00:07:27.710
Calm down.

00:07:27.710 --> 00:07:29.430
Calm down!

00:07:29.870 --> 00:07:33.400
It was so hot that I couldn't sleep, so I just stayed in my boxers...

00:07:33.400 --> 00:07:36.610
Then lock the front door at least.

00:07:37.040 --> 00:07:41.320
By the way, weren't you with Capeta?

00:07:41.320 --> 00:07:44.820
Huh?  W-What do you mean, together?

00:07:44.820 --> 00:07:47.170
At the circuit in Sendai.

00:07:47.170 --> 00:07:49.030
It's the day of the race, right?

00:07:49.030 --> 00:07:51.460
Capeta left early this morning.

00:07:51.460 --> 00:07:53.420
What?!

00:07:57.200 --> 00:07:58.830
<i>Sendai?!</i>

00:07:59.780 --> 00:08:02.550
<i>I didn't hear a thing about it!</i>

00:08:10.680 --> 00:08:12.050
It's gone!

00:08:12.050 --> 00:08:13.880
The <i>Momotarou</i> is gone!

00:08:13.880 --> 00:08:15.770
The <i>Momotarou</i> ?

00:08:15.770 --> 00:08:18.220
It's the new machine we borrowed from Momotarou.

00:08:18.220 --> 00:08:19.820
It's gone.

00:08:23.770 --> 00:08:25.120
As I thought!

00:08:25.120 --> 00:08:26.670
The van is gone, too.

00:08:26.670 --> 00:08:29.490
He's thinking of entering the race
 with his body like that!

00:08:29.490 --> 00:08:32.200
But, if it's not Ca-chan's dad...

00:08:32.200 --> 00:08:35.080
Then who's driving?

00:08:35.080 --> 00:08:37.290
Boss?!

00:08:38.110 --> 00:08:41.010
I'm sorry, on your day off...

00:08:41.010 --> 00:08:44.180
I was just thinking of borrowing the van, but I ended up asking you to drive as well.

00:08:44.180 --> 00:08:48.720
I wanted to watch a go-kart race after such a long time anyway.

00:08:49.520 --> 00:08:51.430
You don't have to worry.

00:08:51.430 --> 00:08:53.390
Look.  We're on time.

00:08:53.390 --> 00:08:55.440
Thank you very much.

00:08:58.120 --> 00:09:01.050
<b>ICA class session is now finished.</b>

00:09:01.050 --> 00:09:02.580
<b>Next will be the FA class.</b>

00:09:02.580 --> 00:09:04.570
<b>Please get ready to enter the course.</b>

00:09:11.250 --> 00:09:14.210
You can get it back in the time trials.

00:09:14.830 --> 00:09:16.670
And then start from pole position.

00:09:17.950 --> 00:09:19.630
Hurry up and get your feelings in order.

00:09:20.650 --> 00:09:21.630
Yes.

00:09:24.340 --> 00:09:26.230
Did you see that, Pops?

00:09:26.230 --> 00:09:29.460
You still think Taira is better than me?

00:09:30.180 --> 00:09:32.420
Hmm?  How about it?

00:09:32.420 --> 00:09:33.980
Why don't you say someth—

00:09:38.150 --> 00:09:39.680
What's the matter, Ryou?

00:09:47.540 --> 00:09:48.780
Taira.

00:09:57.290 --> 00:09:58.510
It's Taira.

00:09:58.510 --> 00:10:00.000
Why is Taira here?

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:01.290
What's he here for?

00:10:01.980 --> 00:10:04.210
Boss, could you please help me?

00:10:04.210 --> 00:10:05.920
Y-Yeah.

00:10:12.250 --> 00:10:13.810
Capeta-kun.

00:10:15.080 --> 00:10:17.770
<i>Why is Capeta-kun here?</i>

00:10:33.660 --> 00:10:35.540
<i>A new machine?!</i>

00:10:35.950 --> 00:10:38.830
<i>Do you really have the confidence to beat him?</i>

00:10:44.000 --> 00:10:45.000
It's Taira!

00:10:45.000 --> 00:10:46.020
Taira?

00:10:46.020 --> 00:10:47.210
Why is Taira...?

00:10:47.210 --> 00:10:49.800
Didn't he break his ribs?

00:10:49.800 --> 00:10:50.510
It's really Taira.

00:10:50.510 --> 00:10:51.430
You're kidding.

00:10:54.100 --> 00:10:58.560
<i>What's with everyone changing color the moment they see Capeta?</i>

00:10:59.860 --> 00:11:01.760
Hey, it's a new machine.

00:11:03.280 --> 00:11:04.660
<i>I see.</i>

00:11:04.660 --> 00:11:07.230
<i>Everyone here...</i>

00:11:07.990 --> 00:11:09.950
<i>hates you that much, huh?</i>

00:11:15.330 --> 00:11:19.290
If Capeta-kun is going to drive,
I'm going out on the course again!

00:11:19.290 --> 00:11:21.210
Calm down.

00:11:21.210 --> 00:11:23.460
The ICA finished a while back.

00:11:26.050 --> 00:11:28.600
Well, I'll be going.

00:11:28.600 --> 00:11:30.530
Yeah.  Give it all you got.

00:11:35.160 --> 00:11:36.090
<i>How about this?</i>

00:11:36.090 --> 00:11:38.390
<i>This tense atmosphere.</i>

00:11:39.070 --> 00:11:41.600
<i>It changed the moment Capeta-kun showed up.</i>

00:11:42.500 --> 00:11:46.400
<i>Capeta-kun sure is an interesting kid.</i>

00:11:54.980 --> 00:11:56.860
Here you go, Young Master.

00:11:56.860 --> 00:11:58.140
Thank you.

00:11:59.500 --> 00:12:01.400
11th place, huh?

00:12:03.970 --> 00:12:06.970
Looks like I wasn't aggressive enough.

00:12:09.060 --> 00:12:10.480
It's not like me.

00:12:11.450 --> 00:12:13.430
Was the next race at Tokaji?

00:12:14.620 --> 00:12:16.590
Yes it is.

00:12:16.590 --> 00:12:18.440
But Young Master...

00:12:18.440 --> 00:12:23.300
it must be very hard traveling to all the circuits around the world.

00:12:23.300 --> 00:12:25.290
It can't be helped.

00:12:25.290 --> 00:12:29.710
A lot of fans around the world are looking forward to seeing me drive.

00:12:35.650 --> 00:12:37.440
Hi, Capeta-kun.

00:12:37.440 --> 00:12:40.290
I was getting worried since I didn't see you around.

00:12:41.890 --> 00:12:43.370
I'm sorry.

00:12:43.880 --> 00:12:46.840
Yo!  We meet again, Reinhart III.

00:12:49.020 --> 00:12:50.540
W-What's going on?

00:12:50.540 --> 00:12:52.700
He's talking to Momotarou.

00:12:52.700 --> 00:12:55.470
Why is he talking to a non-competitive driver...?

00:12:59.260 --> 00:13:02.680
<i>So that's Capeta's fan, huh?</i>

00:13:03.160 --> 00:13:08.190
By the way, that's my Peach Star #1
 that I lent to you, isn't it?

00:13:08.190 --> 00:13:14.350
I can't wait to see you drive in my new machine today.

00:13:16.180 --> 00:13:17.870
U-Umm...

00:13:19.950 --> 00:13:23.160
Thanks for lending me your important kart.

00:13:23.160 --> 00:13:27.040
However, I can't compete in today's race.

00:13:28.610 --> 00:13:30.980
Do your ribs still hurt?

00:13:32.100 --> 00:13:35.200
Well... that too, but...

00:13:36.640 --> 00:13:40.230
There's a match in August that I really want to win.

00:13:40.230 --> 00:13:41.470
That's why—

00:13:41.980 --> 00:13:44.270
I understand.

00:13:44.270 --> 00:13:48.830
It must be something really important that you're sacrificing today's race for.

00:13:48.830 --> 00:13:54.190
After all, sometimes it's important for the warrior to take a rest before a crucial battle.

00:13:54.740 --> 00:13:57.800
Well that's how it is, so I'll give this back to you.

00:13:57.800 --> 00:14:00.570
Thanks a lot.

00:14:00.570 --> 00:14:01.160
See ya.

00:14:03.580 --> 00:14:04.420
<i>Nobu.</i>

00:14:04.420 --> 00:14:06.120
<i>This is okay, right?</i>

00:14:06.120 --> 00:14:08.620
The boss isn't fair.

00:14:08.620 --> 00:14:11.550
Taking only Capeta to Sendai.

00:14:11.550 --> 00:14:16.130
I have work, so the boss took him instead.

00:14:16.130 --> 00:14:20.550
If it was to return the kart, he could have waited until Momotarou came back.

00:14:20.550 --> 00:14:21.750
Sendai.  Sendai.  Sendai.  Sendai!

00:14:21.750 --> 00:14:22.860
Sendai.  Sendai.  Sendai.  Sendai!

00:14:22.860 --> 00:14:24.090
Sendai.  Sendai.  Sendai.  Sendai!

00:14:24.090 --> 00:14:25.180
Sendai.  Sendai.  Sendai.  Sendai!

00:14:25.180 --> 00:14:28.310
How about we all go to Sendai now?

00:14:28.310 --> 00:14:29.270
Miura!

00:14:30.750 --> 00:14:33.980
Sorry, but I can't go to Sendai, Monami-chan.

00:14:47.190 --> 00:14:48.100
Gyuutan, sasakama, zundamochi!

00:14:48.100 --> 00:14:49.120
Gyuutan, sasakama, zundamochi!

00:14:49.120 --> 00:14:51.090
Gyuutan, sasakama, zundamochi!

00:14:51.630 --> 00:14:56.380
Ca-chan, I'm not going to forgive you if you don't bring any gifts back!

00:15:00.670 --> 00:15:05.390
<b>Japan National ICA class time trial
 will begin in five minutes.</b>

00:15:11.170 --> 00:15:12.350
<i>Taira.</i>

00:15:12.350 --> 00:15:13.560
Ryou.

00:15:15.810 --> 00:15:17.840
What was that for, Pops?!

00:15:17.840 --> 00:15:20.080
Taira won't be in today's race.

00:15:20.080 --> 00:15:20.970
Eh?

00:15:20.970 --> 00:15:22.560
Think about it.

00:15:22.560 --> 00:15:25.030
He didn't take the compulsory kart inspection.

00:15:26.250 --> 00:15:28.690
O-Oh yeah, that's right.

00:15:28.690 --> 00:15:30.750
He wasn't here this morning.

00:15:30.750 --> 00:15:34.960
If you calm down and think, you can see things clearly.

00:15:35.980 --> 00:15:37.420
Don't lose your head!

00:15:39.130 --> 00:15:41.880
I got it, Pops.

00:15:46.250 --> 00:15:47.310
<i>Taira.</i>

00:15:51.300 --> 00:15:52.750
<i>I'll do it.</i>

00:15:52.750 --> 00:15:54.860
<i>I'm the fastest!</i>

00:15:56.100 --> 00:15:59.320
<b>Car #7, Shiba Ryou from Garage Hill.</b>

00:15:59.320 --> 00:16:03.620
<b>He turns the last corner and finally goes for the time attack.</b>

00:16:18.430 --> 00:16:19.670
<i>They're fast!</i>

00:16:19.670 --> 00:16:23.930
<i>When did go-karts become this fast?</i>

00:16:24.550 --> 00:16:27.810
<i>They weren't exaggerating about the Nationals.</i>

00:16:33.880 --> 00:16:34.810
<i>Taira.</i>

00:16:37.830 --> 00:16:39.030
<i>You just watch.</i>

00:16:39.030 --> 00:16:43.030
<i>I'll prove to you that I'm faster than you.</i>

00:16:51.660 --> 00:16:53.160
<i>Oh no!</i>

00:16:55.710 --> 00:16:56.210
<b>Oh no!</b>

00:16:56.210 --> 00:16:59.670
<b>Garage Hill's Shiba has gone way off course!</b>

00:16:58.420 --> 00:16:59.670
That idiot!

00:17:00.980 --> 00:17:03.010
<b>What just happened?</b>

00:17:03.010 --> 00:17:05.360
<b>Did he get too excited?</b>

00:17:07.640 --> 00:17:09.050
<i>Damn it!</i>

00:17:09.860 --> 00:17:14.010
<b>He somehow got back on the course,
but this is a painful mistake in the time attack.</b>

00:17:14.010 --> 00:17:15.710
<i>He's still driving.</i>

00:17:15.710 --> 00:17:19.520
<i>There's nothing wrong with him after flying that far out?</i>

00:17:20.040 --> 00:17:24.280
<i>Then what kind of situation would it take to break your ribs?</i>

00:17:24.280 --> 00:17:27.890
Shiba got overly conscious of Taira.

00:17:27.890 --> 00:17:30.500
No, it's not just Shiba.

00:17:30.500 --> 00:17:34.250
It's like everyone's been swallowed up by Taira.

00:17:34.640 --> 00:17:41.280
He's not even competing today, yet it looks as though everyone is conscious of him.

00:17:43.150 --> 00:17:46.220
<i>Everyone is conscious of Capeta?</i>

00:17:53.510 --> 00:17:56.940
<i>So it wasn't like they all hated you.</i>

00:17:58.880 --> 00:18:02.110
<i>Could it be that you're an incredible person or something?</i>

00:18:05.180 --> 00:18:08.070
I bet he really wants to drive now.

00:18:09.980 --> 00:18:14.080
Anyway, we have to do something about the audition fees for Formula Stellar.

00:18:18.970 --> 00:18:20.620
Leave everything to me.

00:18:22.990 --> 00:18:26.420
I'll get Ca-chan into the race, whatever it takes.

00:18:34.850 --> 00:18:38.670
<i>Because I'm the coach of Team Capeta.</i>

00:19:07.380 --> 00:19:13.290
<b>Minamoto Naomi from Autohouse wins by a large margin, not letting anyone near him!</b>

00:19:14.220 --> 00:19:15.750
<b>He is truly undefeatable!</b>

00:19:15.750 --> 00:19:18.180
<b>You can feel the presence of the champion.</b>

00:19:18.590 --> 00:19:19.650
That's him.

00:19:20.580 --> 00:19:22.180
The one I talked to you about.

00:19:22.180 --> 00:19:24.720
The one I would like to beat one day.

00:19:26.150 --> 00:19:28.030
I can't see.

00:19:42.540 --> 00:19:47.430
I want to get into the Formula class so I can fight him!

00:20:00.710 --> 00:20:03.230
Thank you so much for today.

00:20:03.820 --> 00:20:08.230
No.  I also had fun today, to be honest.

00:20:11.480 --> 00:20:14.660
It made me realize that you were also fighting.

00:20:16.550 --> 00:20:18.090
I also...

00:20:29.170 --> 00:20:30.670
But it's almost time.

00:20:31.790 --> 00:20:34.890
You go fight in my place.

00:20:37.810 --> 00:20:40.700
<i>Me, become the president of Ikari Pavement?!</i>

00:20:41.350 --> 00:20:44.320
Your thoughts are going off on a complete tangent, aren't they?

00:20:46.560 --> 00:20:49.310
I'm saying I'll give you the money for the audition.

00:22:50.860 --> 00:22:51.790
Wow!

00:22:51.790 --> 00:22:54.330
Am I really going on this machine?!

00:22:54.330 --> 00:22:56.030
What are you scared of?

00:22:56.030 --> 00:22:57.340
You'll be just fine!

00:22:57.340 --> 00:22:59.910
Make sure to get that scholarship!

00:22:59.910 --> 00:23:00.970
Next time, on Capeta.

00:23:00.970 --> 00:23:02.320
Formula Stellar!

00:23:02.320 --> 00:23:05.240
Now's the time to break the limit!
